<article class="msc-learn-source"><h3>Crypto Asset Custody Basics for Retail Investors - Investor Bulletin</h3><ul><li><strong>author or publisher:</strong> SEC Office of Investor Education and Assistance</li><li><strong>url:</strong> [https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/general-resources/news-alerts/alerts-bulletins/investor-bulletins/crypto-asset-custody-basics-retail-investors-investor-bulletin-0](https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/general-resources/news-alerts/alerts-bulletins/investor-bulletins/crypto-asset-custody-basics-retail-investors-investor-bulletin-0)</li><li><strong>published:</strong> December 12, 2025</li><li><strong>accessed:</strong> July 30, 2026</li><li><strong>supports:</strong> The distinction between self-custody and third-party custody, common hot and cold storage labels, and custody-related operational and insolvency questions.</li><li><strong>limitation:</strong> This is SEC staff investor education, not a Commission rule, provider assessment, or guarantee that any custody model is safe.</li></ul></article>
